    "name": "Farmer Registry API Collection",
    "description": "Staff-API load and smoke requests for the OpenG2P Farmer Registry (dev), mirroring the Locust scenarios in `farmer-registry/performance-testing/locust/api` (register read, change request, intake create). Run with the Postman runner or Newman.\n\n**Hosts (dev).** Staff API `https://staff-farmer-development.oanstaging.com` (the portal host `farmer-registry-development.oanstaging.com` serves only the UI; API paths there return the HTML page with HTTP 200). Keycloak `https://keycloak-development.oanstaging.com`, realm `staff`.\n\n**Auth.** Every call needs a bearer token *and* a CSRF double-submit (same value in the `X-CSRF-Token` cookie and header). The collection pre-request script reuses the `X-CSRF-Token` cookie already in the Postman cookie jar for the host (the server may set its own), or creates one, then sets the header to match and writes the cookie to the jar. Get the token with *0.1*. No token or password is stored in this collection: keep credentials in your own environment, as current values.\n\n**Troubleshooting G2P-AUT-403 CSRF token missing or invalid.** Run requests from this collection (the script lives here, not on single requests); use the Postman desktop app or the Desktop Agent, since the web agent cannot send cookies; clear the host's cookies and `CSRF_TOKEN` if it persists.\n\n**Success check.** Each request asserts HTTP < 400 and `response_header.response_status != ERROR`, because validation errors arrive as HTTP 200.\n\n**Order.** Run in order: the 1.x requests store the farmer that the 2.x requests change; 3.x is independent.\n\n**Not included.** Partner-API ingestion: its Locust flow is still a placeholder (see `performance-testing/README.md`), it needs signed partner requests, and its host has no public DNS on dev.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "_exporter_id": "59130667",
    "_collection_link": "https://go.postman.co/collection/49316197-781ed4fd-859b-4d4b-b387-389077e602d6?source=collection_link"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "0.1 Get Access Token (Keycloak password grant)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('token issued', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "const json = pm.response.json();",
              "if (json.access_token) {",
              "    pm.collectionVariables.set('ACCESS_TOKEN', json.access_token);",
              "    console.log(`ACCESS_TOKEN set, expires in ${json.expires_in}s`);",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "auth": {
          "type": "noauth"
        },
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/x-www-form-urlencoded"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "urlencoded",
          "urlencoded": [
            {
              "key": "grant_type",
              "value": "password"
            },
            {
              "key": "client_id",
              "value": "{{OIDC_CLIENT_ID}}"
            },
            {
              "key": "client_secret",
              "value": "{{OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET}}"
            },
            {
              "key": "username",
              "value": "{{OIDC_USERNAME}}"
            },
            {
              "key": "password",
              "value": "{{OIDC_PASSWORD}}"
            }
          ]
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{KEYCLOAK_BASE}}/realms/{{KEYCLOAK_REALM}}/protocol/openid-connect/token",
          "host": [
            "{{KEYCLOAK_BASE}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "realms",
            "{{KEYCLOAK_REALM}}",
            "protocol",
            "openid-connect",
            "token"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Gets an access token from Keycloak (password grant) and stores it in ACCESS_TOKEN. Put OIDC_USERNAME, OIDC_PASSWORD and OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET in your own Postman environment, never in the collection. The secret is in Keycloak: realm staff > Clients > farmer-registry-staff-portal > Credentials. If the client does not allow the password grant, log in to the portal, copy the X-Access-Token cookie value, and set it as the ACCESS_TOKEN current value instead."
      },
      "response": []
    },
